WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:04.870
When they were about to face down all manner
of things worse than anyone’s deepest, darkest

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:09.590
nightmares, Alex and the rest of the team
did what they could to keep their spirits

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:10.590
up.

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:15.200
There was an old song they used to hum whenever
heading on missions, the low sound of that

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.730
tune giving them just a marginal boost to
their morale.

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:24.660
It never did all that much to numb the sense
of impending doom the team all collectively

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:29.449
felt, but it was better than sitting in a
transport unit in silence, letting the dread

00:00:29.449 --> 00:00:30.679
get to them.

00:00:30.679 --> 00:00:34.280
Even though it had been a while since Mobile
Task Force Epsilon had been dispatched on

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:39.469
their current assignment, and they had hummed
it together as they shipped out, Alex found

00:00:39.469 --> 00:00:42.940
himself trying to remember the words to that
old song.

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:49.269
‘Smile through your fear and sorrow, then
maybe tomorrow you'll see the sun come shining

00:00:49.269 --> 00:00:50.269
through.’

00:00:50.269 --> 00:00:55.839
It was pretty hard for Alex to keep a smile
on his face after losing so many of his teammates…

00:00:55.839 --> 00:00:59.170
and seeing what The Grinner had done to them.

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:04.629
The trail had gone cold again, much to the
disdain of the team’s commanding officer.

00:01:04.629 --> 00:01:09.710
Receiving a number of new sightings and witness
reports, the SCP Foundation had sent the remaining

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:15.101
members of MTF Epsilon – also known under
the code name ‘Tyrfing Black’ – out

00:01:15.101 --> 00:01:18.640
on another hunt for SCP-4910.

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:22.950
The creature had been at large for years now,
with every attempt the Foundation had made

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:26.399
to capture it ending in grisly, gut-churning
failure.

00:01:26.399 --> 00:01:30.619
Fifty-seven separate times they had sent their
personnel after this anomaly on the loose,

00:01:30.619 --> 00:01:33.350
and not all of them had come back.

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:37.710
Although Alex often found himself thinking
of the ones that had returned, and seeing

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:42.310
photos of how they had changed in the after-action
reports.

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:44.720
Not to mention the bodies.

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:49.590
Those that made it back ended up looking virtually
unrecognizable as human beings.

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:53.979
After having seen what happened to them, maybe
it was better not to know what gruesome fate

00:01:53.979 --> 00:01:59.020
had befallen the ones who were still missing
in action, he told himself, keeping that train

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:00.920
of thought private.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:06.300
Tracking SCP-4910 brought its own plethora
of issues; naturally, or the Foundation would

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:07.840
have it secured by now.

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:12.290
The creature had some way of interfering with
recording devices, rendering them completely

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:13.620
useless.

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:19.360
And of course, that meant that Tyrfing Black
had little to no clue what the monster actually

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:20.530
looked like.

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:26.070
Given that it disrupted any and all recording
equipment, including cameras and audio devices,

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:28.990
the Task Force’s hands were somewhat tied.

00:02:28.990 --> 00:02:34.750
It forced Alex and his teammates to try and
locate it through more old-fashioned means,

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:39.580
following up on eyewitness reports, a lot
of which led them to a dead end.

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:43.390
Every now and then, however, one of these
sightings would prove to be genuine.

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:47.260
The quickest way to tell was usually if a
person living near the place where a report

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:49.860
came in from had gone missing lately.

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:55.890
Civilians were SCP-4910’s main source of
food, and a recent disappearance in the area,

00:02:55.890 --> 00:03:00.450
paired with a sighting of something large
and four-legged, usually meant the beast had

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:03.450
come out of hiding to feed again.

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:05.720
“Alright, listen up team!”

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:07.060
Commanding Officer Sawyer announced.

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:12.111
With the level of militaristic speed and discipline
expected of them by the Foundation, Alex and

00:03:12.111 --> 00:03:16.120
the other members of the Mobile Task Force
quickly filed out of the transport and fell

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:18.780
in, ready and waiting to receive their orders.

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:23.970
“Now, you all know the reason why we’re
here,” Sawyer strode back and forth, arms

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:28.700
behind his back as he addressed what was left
of his unit; three operatives, not including

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:29.700
himself.

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:33.820
“Even so, it’s imperative you don’t
forget it either.

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:35.660
So, these are the facts.

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:41.340
To date, the anomaly designated as SCP-4910
is still running wild.

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:45.340
But if we have anything to say about it, then
that sucker won’t be running for much longer!”

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:51.480
The three troops gave a quick chant in agreement,
although Alex kept quiet, just mouthing along.

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:56.310
He wasn’t exactly sure that they would actually
ever catch up to The Grinner.

00:03:56.310 --> 00:04:00.470
So little file footage of the monster even
existed, meaning the team still had little

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:06.110
to no clue what this thing was, or if they
were even equipped to fight it.

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:12.220
And then again, a huge part of him didn’t
want to ever find SCP-4910, knowing what it

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:16.170
had done to the fallen former members of Mobile
Task Force Epsilon.

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:21.109
“So, here’s the latest,” Commander Sawyer
continued, silencing the team.

00:04:21.109 --> 00:04:25.520
“Approximately twelve hours ago, we received
a message from one of the Foundation’s field

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:26.520
operatives.

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:30.729
This agent has been in deep cover living in
a nearby town for a number of years.”

00:04:30.729 --> 00:04:35.939
As he spoke, the commanding officer gestured
down the high ridge that they had landed on.

00:04:35.939 --> 00:04:40.020
Far below, sitting in the center of a huge
dip in the earth, was a small township.

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:44.270
There was barely enough room for more than
a few hundred people at most.

00:04:44.270 --> 00:04:49.539
All around the small urban center, bordering
the entire town in an almost perfect circle,

00:04:49.539 --> 00:04:50.819
was a dense forest.

00:04:50.819 --> 00:04:55.889
It was an ideal cover for the monster, and
Alex could see on his teammate’s faces that

00:04:55.889 --> 00:04:57.800
they all knew it too.

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:02.379
With them in the town, there was no way they
could cover every possible avenue of approach.

00:05:02.379 --> 00:05:06.139
“This operative, is he the one that called
in the eyewitness report?”

00:05:06.139 --> 00:05:08.819
one of the team, Warren, piped up and asked.

00:05:08.819 --> 00:05:11.939
“That’s correct, Agent Warren,” Sawyer
confirmed.

00:05:11.939 --> 00:05:15.930
“That agent has agreed to meet us at a rendezvous
a few clicks north of here.

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:20.439
The four of us will circumnavigate the town,
stick to the cover of these woods as we head

00:05:20.439 --> 00:05:22.090
out to make contact with him.

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:24.810
From there, he’ll guide us to where the
creature was sighted.”

00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:30.719
The team gave little response, just a few
low murmurs expressing their collective apprehension.

00:05:30.719 --> 00:05:34.979
In a strange way, Alex found it comforting
that, at the very least, he wasn’t the only

00:05:34.979 --> 00:05:40.319
one having some serious reservations about
potentially coming face to face with SCP-4910.

00:05:40.319 --> 00:05:44.110
“Now, boys,” their commander sighed.

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:46.039
“I get it.

00:05:46.039 --> 00:05:50.159
All of us have been trying to catch this freak
for a long while, and we’ve lost a lot of

00:05:50.159 --> 00:05:52.520
good people from our unit along the way.

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:55.400
But we are Tyrfing Black, you hear me?

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:57.470
You all know what that name means.

00:05:57.470 --> 00:06:02.319
Tyrfing, as in the sword from Norse Mythology,
cursed to kill every time it was drawn.

00:06:02.319 --> 00:06:09.180
And that’s us, that is exactly what we’re
going to do when we finally find that monster.

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:11.659
For all our fallen brothers and sisters.

00:06:11.659 --> 00:06:15.690
By the time we’re through with it, The Grinner
will be smiling out of the other side of its

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:16.699
ugly face.

00:06:16.699 --> 00:06:18.800
Now, let’s move out, double time!”

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:22.520
With a half-hearted cheer, the squad prepared
to start their hike through the forest that

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:23.990
encircled the town.

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:28.909
The four survivors of Mobile Task Force Epsilon
fanned out, keeping close enough to see and

00:06:28.909 --> 00:06:32.340
hear each other, but not too close that they
were clustered together.

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:36.759
The more they huddled up, the easier it would
be to take them out if The Grinner was able

00:06:36.759 --> 00:06:38.419
to get the jump on them.

00:06:38.419 --> 00:06:42.199
Although he should have been keeping his eyes
forward, looking out for any tracks the creature

00:06:42.199 --> 00:06:46.099
might have left, Alex couldn’t help checking
over his shoulder.

00:06:46.099 --> 00:06:51.340
The sun was getting lower and lower in the
sky, the day rapidly turning to night.

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:56.550
Before long, their visibility would be compromised,
severely limited by the lack of natural light.

00:06:56.550 --> 00:07:01.979
It was then he looked to his fellow team members,
Warren and Jones; besides Alex himself and

00:07:01.979 --> 00:07:06.080
the squad’s commander, they were the only
other Tyrfing Black operatives left.

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:10.139
Warren had always been the more brash and
outspoken of the group, willing to stand up

00:07:10.139 --> 00:07:13.020
and question the orders of Commanding Officer
Sawyer.

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:18.180
Alex could tell Warren was having the same
worries about this plan as he was.

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:22.930
The thick tree line gave them plenty of cover,
but could also easily work to the monster’s

00:07:22.930 --> 00:07:27.520
advantage, allowing it to sneak up and get
the drop on the team with relative ease.

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:32.870
But both Alex and Warren also knew that, if
the MTF was pushed back towards the town,

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:39.620
they would be trapped, like fish in a barrel,
just waiting to be picked off by SCP-4910.

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:44.340
Jones was walking slightly ahead of the others,
his gaze rapidly scanning back and forth across

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:46.020
the forest before them.

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:50.990
He was the team’s most accomplished tracker,
meaning he was always on the lookout for anything

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:56.759
that could give them a better idea as to where
the Grinner was heading, or if it was nearby.

00:07:56.759 --> 00:08:03.089
From scratches on tree bark, to sets of inhuman,
unnatural footprints belonging to a large,

00:08:03.089 --> 00:08:09.309
quadruped beast, and, of course, trails of
blood or bodies, if there was a sign, Jones

00:08:09.309 --> 00:08:10.589
would find it.

00:08:10.589 --> 00:08:14.819
Much like Alex, the other two operatives had
become more than a little jaded with their

00:08:14.819 --> 00:08:17.509
ongoing hunt for the elusive entity.

00:08:17.509 --> 00:08:21.990
But on top of that, not that either one of
them would admit it to the others, they were

00:08:21.990 --> 00:08:23.360
scared of it too.

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:27.589
The things this creature was capable of were
enough to make anyone think twice about wanting

00:08:27.589 --> 00:08:28.680
to find it.

00:08:28.680 --> 00:08:33.210
As much to quell his own fear and sorrow,
as well as that of his teammates, Alex started

00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:38.750
humming the tune to Smile, just loud enough
for them to hear, but quiet enough – he

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:42.110
hoped – to not draw any unwanted attention.

00:08:42.110 --> 00:08:46.230
It was already dark by the time Tyrfing Black
were beginning to approach the coordinates

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:49.230
where they had arranged to meet the Foundation
agent.

00:08:49.230 --> 00:08:53.400
Commander Sawyer had given his troops a silent
hand signal, and all of them had lowered the

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:56.370
night vision goggles affixed to their helmets.

00:08:56.370 --> 00:09:00.480
Through the fuzzy green hue of the optics,
Jones was the first to spot a figure leaning

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:03.890
against a tree, waiting for them in the distance.

00:09:03.890 --> 00:09:08.520
“Sir,” he whispered to Sawyer, catching
his attention and then making a gesture towards

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:11.620
the vaguely human shape in the shadows ahead
of them.

00:09:11.620 --> 00:09:16.380
Looking to where Jones had pointed, Alex and
Warren could see the agent waiting for them.

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:20.150
Following their commander’s lead, they paced
steadily towards the undercover operative…

00:09:20.150 --> 00:09:24.870
it was only as they stepped closer that they
realized he wasn’t moving.

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:26.160
“Agent Manning?”

00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:30.560
Sawyer called out to him, trying to keep his
voice as hushed and low as possible.

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:34.660
No response, Manning was still, propped up
against a tree trunk.

00:09:34.660 --> 00:09:38.740
The team were a few feet from him now, while
the commander stepped up to the agent and

00:09:38.740 --> 00:09:40.850
turned him around by his shoulder…

00:09:40.850 --> 00:09:42.880
only to recoil at what he saw.

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:46.390
Manning’s eyes were open but remained unblinking
and lifeless.

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:50.290
But that was far from the worst thing that
had happened to his face.

00:09:50.290 --> 00:09:55.670
A huge, disproportionate grin had stretched
his mouth wider than was natural.

00:09:55.670 --> 00:10:00.570
Masses of jagged, uneven teeth had taken root,
pushing out from under his tongue and the

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:06.050
roof of his mouth, filling his airway with
thick clusters of yellowy white enamel.

00:10:06.050 --> 00:10:11.280
There were so many new teeth sprouting from
Manning’s face that new fixed and unsettling

00:10:11.280 --> 00:10:15.800
smiles had started to form, splitting open
his cheeks.

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:19.810
“Back, back!” Sawyer told his men in an
urgent, hushed whisper.

00:10:19.810 --> 00:10:23.500
“Remember boys, we don’t know how contagious
this thing is.”

00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:27.440
Given they had never seen it in the flesh,
that was true.

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:32.390
All the previous failed attempts at bringing
in SCP-4910 had ended with victims displaying

00:10:32.390 --> 00:10:36.380
similar signs of some unknown anomalous infection.

00:10:36.380 --> 00:10:40.350
Whatever it was, it seemed to spread from
the creature itself, causing a human being

00:10:40.350 --> 00:10:43.020
to overproduce masses of teeth.

00:10:43.020 --> 00:10:46.880
This started with new clusters of dentins
painfully tearing through the mouth until

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:50.190
the victim could no longer speak or breathe
properly.

00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:56.100
If given enough time, teeth would begin forming
elsewhere on the body, below the neck in places

00:10:56.100 --> 00:10:57.360
they shouldn’t be.

00:10:57.360 --> 00:11:01.790
The lucky ones – not that there were many
of them – had managed to get themselves

00:11:01.790 --> 00:11:05.260
medical attention soon after they had been
exposed.

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:11.390
Within an hour, maybe two at best, of an encounter
with SCP-4910, there was still a chance of

00:11:11.390 --> 00:11:15.070
saving one of its victims through intensive
dental surgery.

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:19.200
But three or four hours afterward, and it
would already be too late.

00:11:19.200 --> 00:11:23.780
Hearing the distant snap of a twig, Jones
turned with his weapon raised, arms locked

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:25.540
in a combat-ready stance.

00:11:25.540 --> 00:11:30.340
“Possible contact,” he declared, aiming
his gun into the deep, shadowy forest.

00:11:30.340 --> 00:11:34.540
Matching his bearing and targeting the same
area, Sawyer gave a hand signal to Alex and

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:37.020
Warren, urging them to lock and load.

00:11:37.020 --> 00:11:42.710
Lifting their rifles, they covered the opposite
direction, just in case someone, or something

00:11:42.710 --> 00:11:46.240
came dashing out of the forest at them from
the other direction.

00:11:46.240 --> 00:11:52.530
For a few moments, everything was still, although
certainly not calm in the least part.

00:11:52.530 --> 00:11:56.550
Feeling a bead of sweat crawl down the back
of his neck, Alex lifted a hand to wipe his

00:11:56.550 --> 00:12:02.720
face clean, the only sound being the low,
panting breaths of the four MTF agents.

00:12:02.720 --> 00:12:08.330
That was when he saw a shadow move, just ahead
of him, darting between the trees before vanishing

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:10.400
from the view of his optics once again.

00:12:10.400 --> 00:12:15.490
It was at least the size of a horse, far bigger
than Alex had been expected, and able to move

00:12:15.490 --> 00:12:18.200
around astonishingly fast on its four legs.

00:12:18.200 --> 00:12:21.550
“Movement this side,” he announced, alerting
his teammates.

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:24.040
“It’s toying with us,” Sawyer muttered.

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:26.160
“With respect, how’s that possible sir?”

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:27.160
Warren asked.

00:12:27.160 --> 00:12:28.720
“It’s an animal, isn’t it?”

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:30.540
“It’s a hunter,” Jones replied.

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:35.240
“We need to move, our visibility’s no
good with all these trees around,” the commander

00:12:35.240 --> 00:12:36.240
whispered.

00:12:36.240 --> 00:12:38.840
“On my mark, we make our way towards the
town.”

00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:42.600
“But, sir, we’ll be sitting ducks down
there, it can flank us from any side,” Warren

00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:43.600
argued.

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:46.230
“We’re better off down there, at least
we’d have streetlights to help us see it

00:12:46.230 --> 00:12:47.230
coming!”

00:12:47.230 --> 00:12:51.520
Alex interjected, mainly just making an excuse
to get as far away from the encroaching entity

00:12:51.520 --> 00:12:52.520
as possible.

00:12:52.520 --> 00:12:55.830
“This isn’t up for discussion,” Sawyer
said, taking command.

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:57.800
“Head for the town, that’s an order.

00:12:57.800 --> 00:13:00.240
On my count, three, two…”

00:13:00.240 --> 00:13:01.240
“Contact!”

00:13:01.240 --> 00:13:02.240
Jones shouted.

00:13:02.240 --> 00:13:06.190
The deafening noise and blinding muzzle flash
of his weapon firing quickly followed as he

00:13:06.190 --> 00:13:09.900
sprayed bullets wildly at a shape that was
barrelling through the forest towards the

00:13:09.900 --> 00:13:10.900
team.

00:13:10.900 --> 00:13:14.720
Alex turned to see what was happening, only
for Sawyer to yell at the top of his voice,

00:13:14.720 --> 00:13:16.040
almost drowned out by the gunfire.

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:18.440
“Go, get out of here, now!”

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:22.090
Obeying his orders, Alex turned his heels
and sprinted towards the low orange light

00:13:22.090 --> 00:13:25.770
of the nearby town, just visible at the edge
of the tree line.

00:13:25.770 --> 00:13:30.050
Warren was next to him, matching his speed,
their heavy tactical gear that was strapped

00:13:30.050 --> 00:13:35.160
to their bodies jostling back and forth each
time one foot came down on the forest floor.

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:40.030
Glancing back over his shoulder, Alex saw
Jones had ceased fire and was running up behind

00:13:40.030 --> 00:13:41.030
them.

00:13:41.030 --> 00:13:44.010
Further back was Sawyer… with The Grinner
bearing down on him.

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:48.630
The commanding officer of Tyrfing Black had
his weapon raised, finger squeezing down on

00:13:48.630 --> 00:13:49.640
the trigger.

00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:53.180
Every round he fired illuminated part of the
forest for a split second.

00:13:53.180 --> 00:13:57.370
Alex couldn’t make out the creature in any
great detail, not while also running further

00:13:57.370 --> 00:14:00.230
and further away, increasing his distance
from it.

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:05.680
All he could make out from this far was a
pink, fleshy quadrupedal mass galloping straight

00:14:05.680 --> 00:14:06.970
for Sawyer.

00:14:06.970 --> 00:14:11.920
He was yelling to get SCP-4910’s attention,
the sound of his war cries carrying over the

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:13.070
night air.

00:14:13.070 --> 00:14:17.350
As the three MTF agents broke through the
treeline and reached the edge of the forest,

00:14:17.350 --> 00:14:22.890
their commander’s shouts quickly turned
into screams of intense pain and unspeakable

00:14:22.890 --> 00:14:25.740
horror, and then fell silent.

00:14:25.740 --> 00:14:30.910
Alex wasn’t sure if the creature had attacked
and eaten him, or caused more of those unnatural

00:14:30.910 --> 00:14:35.780
teeth to fill Sawyer’s mouth, blocking his
screams permanently.

00:14:35.780 --> 00:14:41.030
Reaching the town, every road was completely
deserted, gently lit by the dim glow of orange

00:14:41.030 --> 00:14:42.380
streetlights.

00:14:42.380 --> 00:14:47.620
Tiny rural stores and independent businesses
had their doors bolted tight, roll-down shutters

00:14:47.620 --> 00:14:52.020
locked up for the night, meaning hiding in
one of the buildings wasn’t an option.

00:14:52.020 --> 00:14:56.130
Panting, Alex leaned over and put his hands
to his knees, trying desperately to catch

00:14:56.130 --> 00:14:58.030
his breath.

00:14:58.030 --> 00:14:59.940
“Now what?”

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:04.200
Warren asked, the terror in his voice impossible
to miss.

00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:06.620
“That thing’s gonna be here any second.”

00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:10.510
“We need to get away from here, as fast
as we can, and send word to the Foundation,”

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:14.490
Alex answered, speaking between deep, breathless
wheezes.

00:15:14.490 --> 00:15:19.200
“Tell them we need back up, that this thing
is too dangerous for only three of us to take

00:15:19.200 --> 00:15:20.200
on.”

00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:23.910
“There may not be enough time for that,”
Jones chimed in, standing a few paces away

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:24.910
from the others.

00:15:24.910 --> 00:15:28.670
He had been staring down the long stretch
of the street they had stopped at, frozen

00:15:28.670 --> 00:15:31.180
to the spot, barely moving a muscle.

00:15:31.180 --> 00:15:35.540
Both Alex and Warren turned to look in the
same direction… and there it was, only a

00:15:35.540 --> 00:15:38.350
few feet away under the light of a streetlamp.

00:15:38.350 --> 00:15:44.120
It was almost like SCP-4910 was waiting for
them to catch their breath, intelligent enough

00:15:44.120 --> 00:15:46.870
to know its hunt wasn’t yet over.

00:15:46.870 --> 00:15:52.120
Alex, having now finally got a better look
at the monster, instantly wished he hadn’t.

00:15:52.120 --> 00:15:56.590
It made him feel sick, like there was a lump
lodged in the back of his throat.

00:15:56.590 --> 00:16:03.260
The Grinner stood atop four pink, sinewy legs,
its body just a formless mass of pure musculature

00:16:03.260 --> 00:16:07.300
that looked like it had been sculpted out
of the same tissue that human gums are made

00:16:07.300 --> 00:16:08.300
from.

00:16:08.300 --> 00:16:13.340
It lacked a neck, instead having a pair of
massive jaws poking out between its front

00:16:13.340 --> 00:16:18.300
shoulders, a dark, marble-like eye on either
side of its head.

00:16:18.300 --> 00:16:23.550
SCP-4910’s wide, almost crocodilian jaws
parted, showing off what had earned it the

00:16:23.550 --> 00:16:25.750
ironic nickname of ‘The Grinner’.

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:31.680
It presented a gaping maw of crooked, uneven
teeth, with more clusters of enamel protruding

00:16:31.680 --> 00:16:34.720
from its back, elbows, and head.

00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:37.740
These teeth even formed the hooves it walked
on.

00:16:37.740 --> 00:16:42.190
At this distance, it was hard to tell if the
sickening yellow coloring of the teeth was

00:16:42.190 --> 00:16:47.130
purely because of the streetlights, or that
they had all been stained and covered in plaque.

00:16:47.130 --> 00:16:50.990
Alex tried to contain a cough in his throat,
his stomach feeling like it was folding over

00:16:50.990 --> 00:16:54.620
itself at the sickening sight of SCP-4910.

00:16:54.620 --> 00:16:59.070
He started spluttering, wondering if he was
about to vomit given the lingering feeling

00:16:59.070 --> 00:17:03.440
at the back of his throat, like that sensation
one gets when something is forcing its way

00:17:03.440 --> 00:17:04.440
up the esophagus.

00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:10.209
But it was lodged, the feeling wasn’t coming
up and out of Alex’s throat, it was stuck

00:17:10.209 --> 00:17:11.209
there.

00:17:11.209 --> 00:17:15.699
By now he was wheezing, desperately trying
to breathe through relentless coughs.

00:17:15.699 --> 00:17:20.629
Jones kept his eyes on the creature; it was
pacing slowly towards them now, keeping a

00:17:20.629 --> 00:17:24.970
distance but moving like a lion encircling
its prey.

00:17:24.970 --> 00:17:29.620
Warren turned and kneeled down to Alex, slapping
him hard on the back, trying to help him cough

00:17:29.620 --> 00:17:32.039
up whatever he was practically choking on.

00:17:32.039 --> 00:17:37.600
Alex’s eyes started going misty, watering
up and he gasped for air, still feeling that

00:17:37.600 --> 00:17:41.799
lingering feeling of being held right at the
edge of being sick.

00:17:41.799 --> 00:17:46.210
In a final act of desperation, he jammed his
fingers down his throat, trying to dislodge

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:48.850
or dispel whatever was making him gag.

00:17:48.850 --> 00:17:55.180
That was when he felt it, a cluster of little,
solid pieces embedded in the roof of his mouth.

00:17:55.180 --> 00:18:01.309
Teeth, teeth that hadn’t been there before,
hadn’t grown naturally but had just sprung

00:18:01.309 --> 00:18:02.789
out of his flesh.

00:18:02.789 --> 00:18:05.200
And more were growing.

00:18:05.200 --> 00:18:11.059
Pain filled his mouth, spreading over Alex’s
entire face as new jagged teeth came bursting

00:18:11.059 --> 00:18:16.350
through his gumline, overlapping with his
natural set, tearing his jaw into a wide,

00:18:16.350 --> 00:18:17.820
crooked grin.

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:21.990
Looking up through his tear-filled eyes, he
could see the same uneven smile on the face

00:18:21.990 --> 00:18:28.159
of the Grinner, as SCP-4910 began dashing
towards its next prey.

00:18:28.159 --> 00:18:35.269
Now go and check out “SCP-323 THE WENDIGO
SKULL” and “SCP-2086 MAN EATING BUS”

00:18:35.269 --> 00:18:41.059
if you dare to learn about even more malicious
monstrosities, carnivorous creatures and atrocious

00:18:41.059 --> 00:18:44.299
anomalies that all seek to do harm to humans!

